{
  "$contract": "Accreditation Intelligence Phase A — the FROZEN wire contract for the three readiness-history endpoints. Backend-first shared fixture (spec D.10): the web engineer codes against THIS file and does not wait for the API. Every payload below is a literal, complete example. HONESTY RULE: the word 'trend' is a route segment only — it never appears in any human-readable string. Phase A reports OBSERVED CHANGE. domainScores is a Phase-B column and is absent from every Phase-A payload.",
  "$endpoints": {
    "series": "GET /schools/:schoolId/accreditation/readiness/series",
    "trend": "GET /schools/:schoolId/accreditation/readiness/trend?seriesKey&from&to&granularity",
    "diff": "GET /schools/:schoolId/accreditation/readiness/diff?seriesKey&from&to"
  },
  "$rules": [
    "seriesKey is the adopted framework CODE, or the literal string 'none' for standards linked to no framework. It is NEVER the read-time dominant-framework heuristic.",
    "requiresSelection === (series.length > 1). defaultSeriesKey = the series with the most leaves; tie → seriesKey ascending.",
    "Documented (selfScoredPct, the rubric term) and Defensible (verifiedPct, the evidence term) are ALWAYS rendered as a pair. readinessPct alone is never a headline.",
    "change.available === false → change.from / change.to / change.deltaPct are all null and change.reason is a non-null sentence rendered VERBATIM. No arrow, no direction word.",
    "decomposition is non-null only when points.length >= 3 (MIN_POINTS_FOR_DIRECTION); otherwise null.",
    "A break inside [from,to] forces change.direction = 'insufficient_history' and the chart renders a GAP at breaks[].date — not a continuous line. The decomposition is still returned because it EXPLAINS the break (fromScopeChange).",
    "boardMarker is fail-soft: it never returns 402 and never blocks the payload.",
    "demoData is a property of the SERIES, not of one row: it is true when this school's record contains ANY reading written by the env-gated demo seeder. A genuine capture appended on top INHERITS isDemo, so a real night can never launder fabricated history into an unlabelled record. The UI must render a hard DEMO DATA chip.",
    "points: [] has TWO distinct causes and the UI must not conflate them. seriesStartsAt === null (and the /series entry has no pointCount) means nothing was ever recorded — 'tracking starts today'. A non-null seriesStartsAt with an empty points array means readings exist OUTSIDE the requested window (the common multi-framework case: a series the school stopped using more than 365 days ago); saying 'earlier readiness was not recorded' there would be false. See trendWindowEmpty."
  ],
